## Structured Content Endpoints (JSON for AI systems) - Careers section
Clean, machine-readable versions of the Careers section of capgemini.com (global site only), free of navigation, layout and script markup. Same content as the HTML pages; the HTML URL remains canonical. Every Careers page and job page also advertises its JSON document with `<link rel="alternate" type="application/json">` and a `Link` HTTP header.

- Careers page: https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/pages/{path} where {path} is the page's URL path, e.g. https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/pages/careers, https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/pages/careers/why-join-capgemini, https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/pages/careers/career-paths/executives
- Careers - open positions index: https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/jobs?page=1&size=50
- Careers - filtered search: https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/jobs?search={keyword}&country_code={country_code}&location={location}&professional_communities={profession}&contract_type={contract_type}&experience_level={experience_level}&brand={brand}&page={page}&size={size}
  (all parameters optional; each index response describes every parameter and the accepted values under `search_capabilities` and carries `links.next` / `links.prev` to walk every page)
- Careers - single job: https://www.capgemini.com/wp-json/llm/v1/jobs/{id} (the id as on the job page, e.g. 552514-en_GB+sap_btp)

Notes: read-only, GET only, JSON. Each document carries `canonical_url` (the HTML page; cite that URL) and `related_pages` - the Careers navigation (Job Search, Why Join Capgemini, Life at Capgemini, Meet our People, Career Path) with `url` pointing at the JSON document and `html_url` at the page. Links inside documents follow the same rule. A 404 with error code `section_disabled` means the content is temporarily withheld - retry later; `ambiguous_slug` means the full page path is required.
